// A doc comment whose fenced code `gos test` compiles and runs - the
// `lang::doctest` surface. The fence is compiled in the scope of the item it
// documents and calls it; `main` exercises the same function, so the three
// execution tiers run exactly what the doctest documents.

// Adds the doubled second addend, the way the doctest below shows.
//
// ```
// assert_eq(add_doubled(4, 2), 8)
// println("{}", add_doubled(4, 2))
// ```
//
// A `text` fence stays prose and is never compiled:
//
// ```text
// this is not a program
// ```
fn add_doubled(a: i64, b: i64) -> i64 { a + b * 2 }

fn main() {
    println("{}", add_doubled(4, 2))
}
